  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A spring obeys Hooke’s law and has a spring constant <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"k\"></span>.<br/>The spring is extended horizontally. The extension of the spring is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>.<br/>When released, the spring returns to its original length in time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Δ t\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the average power developed by the spring as it returns to its original length?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{k x}{2 Δ t}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{k x}{Δ t}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{k {x}^{2}}{2 Δ t}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{k {x}^{2}}{Δ t}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
